# Lab 20 Experiment 6: Resolve a Package Agent Identity to its Blueprint
#
# Given one Agent 365 Package ID, this read-only experiment resolves:
#
# Package
# -> agentIdentityId
# -> Agent Identity
# -> agentIdentityBlueprintId
# -> tenant-local Blueprint principal
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Add this value to the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_BLUEPRINT_LOOKUP_PACKAGE_ID=<exact-package-id>
#
# The public-client application also needs these approved delegated Microsoft
# Graph permissions with admin consent:
#
# - CopilotPackages.Read.All
# - AgentIdentity.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All
#
# This experiment performs no writes. Do not save authentication responses.
# Save any required Package, Agent Identity, or Blueprint response only under:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/
#
@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@packageId = {{$dotenv A365_BLUEPRINT_LOOKUP_PACKAGE_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@lookupScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Step 1 - Start delegated device-code authentication
#
# Expected: HTTP 200 with user_code, device_code, and verification_uri.
# Complete browser sign-in before running Step 2.
# Never save this response.

# @name blueprintLookupStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{lookupScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 2 - Exchange the device code for a Graph access token
#
# Expected after browser sign-in: HTTP 200 with access_token.
# If Graph returns authorization_pending, finish sign-in, wait for the interval
# from Step 1, and run this request again.
# Never save this response.

# @name blueprintLookupToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{blueprintLookupStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3 - Read the selected Package
#
# Expected: HTTP 200 with the exact Package selected through .env.
#
# Inspect:
# - id
# - displayName
# - platform
# - agentIdentityId
#
# STOP if agentIdentityId is absent, null, or empty. That Package does not
# provide an Agent Identity ID that this experiment can resolve.
#
# Save the response as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/package.json

# @name blueprintLookupPackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{packageId}}?$select=id,displayName,platform,agentIdentityId
Authorization: Bearer {{blueprintLookupToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 4A - Try agentIdentityId as the Agent Identity object ID
#
# The URL uses agentIdentityId directly from the Step 3 response.
#
# Expected: HTTP 200 with:
# - id: Agent Identity object ID
# - displayName: Agent Identity display name
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId: parent Blueprint application ID (appId)
#
# This is the documented Agent Identity GET shape. If it returns
# Request_ResourceNotFound, continue to Step 4B because the public Package
# documentation does not define the semantics of its observed agentIdentityId
# field.
#
# Save the response or safe error body as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/agent-identity-by-object-id.json

# @name blueprintLookupAgentIdentityByObjectId
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{blueprintLookupPackage.response.body.$.agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity?$select=id,appId,displayName,servicePrincipalType,accountEnabled,agentIdentityBlueprintId
Authorization: Bearer {{blueprintLookupToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 4B - If Step 4A returned 404, try agentIdentityId as appId
#
# Microsoft Graph supports addressing a service principal by appId through an
# alternate key. Run this request only when Step 4A returned
# Request_ResourceNotFound.
#
# If this request succeeds:
# - confirm response appId equals the Package agentIdentityId;
# - use this response for Step 5B; and
# - record that the Package field behaved as appId rather than object ID.
#
# If both Step 4A and Step 4B return Request_ResourceNotFound, the Package
# contains an Agent Identity reference that cannot currently be resolved.
#
# If sent, save the response or safe error body as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/agent-identity-by-app-id.json

# @name blueprintLookupAgentIdentityByAppId
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintLookupPackage.response.body.$.agentIdentityId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity?$select=id,appId,displayName,servicePrincipalType,accountEnabled,agentIdentityBlueprintId
Authorization: Bearer {{blueprintLookupToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 5A - Read the Blueprint principal after Step 4A succeeds
#
# agentIdentityBlueprintId from Step 4A is the parent Blueprint application
# appId, not the Blueprint application object ID.
#
# Expected: HTTP 200 with:
# - id: tenant-local Blueprint principal object ID
# - appId: Blueprint application ID
# - displayName: tenant-local Blueprint principal display name
# - accountEnabled: principal state
#
# Confirm that appId exactly matches the Step 4A Agent Identity's
# agentIdentityBlueprintId.
#
# If this branch is used, save the response as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/blueprint-principal-from-object-id.json

# @name blueprintLookupPrincipalFromObjectId
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintLookupAgentIdentityByObjectId.response.body.$.agentIdentityBlueprintId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal?$select=id,appId,displayName,accountEnabled
Authorization: Bearer {{blueprintLookupToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 5B - Read the Blueprint principal after Step 4B succeeds
#
# Run this branch only when Step 4A failed and Step 4B succeeded.
#
# If this branch is used, save the response as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/06-package-blueprint-lookup/blueprint-principal-from-app-id.json

# @name blueprintLookupPrincipalFromAppId
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintLookupAgentIdentityByAppId.response.body.$.agentIdentityBlueprintId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal?$select=id,appId,displayName,accountEnabled
Authorization: Bearer {{blueprintLookupToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Result
#
# The relationship is established only when all of these checks pass:
#
# 1. Step 3 Package id equals A365_BLUEPRINT_LOOKUP_PACKAGE_ID.
# 2. For the Step 4A path, Agent Identity id equals Step 3 agentIdentityId.
# 3. For the Step 4B path, Agent Identity appId equals Step 3 agentIdentityId.
# 4. The selected Step 5 Blueprint principal appId equals the successful
#    Agent Identity response's agentIdentityBlueprintId.
#
# Report these values separately:
#
# - Microsoft platform: Step 3 platform
# - Package ID: Step 3 id
# - Package agentIdentityId and whether it resolved as objectId or appId
# - Agent Identity object ID: successful Step 4 response id
# - Blueprint name: successful Step 5 response displayName
# - Blueprint ID: successful Step 5 response appId
# - Blueprint principal object ID: successful Step 5 response id
#
# Do not interpret the Blueprint principal object ID as the Blueprint ID.
